From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:42:46 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] Plutonium: a floating native window keeps its
 client-side resize edges

EXO-EMBED: <native-window floating> tells the browser (NativeWindowHost::
SetFloating) the page shows the window floating rather than tiled. The
driving element's flag goes to Exo (EmbeddedWindows::SetFloating()), which
then no longer sends the parked window the xdg_toplevel tiled states, so a
client with client-side decorations (GTK 4) keeps its shadow and the resize
edges in it. The element clips the shadow, so those edges got no press:
now, within kResizeEdgeMargin CSS pixels outside a floating element's
content box, the input router asks the renderer
(ForeignFrameSinkDelegate::NearResizeEdge()), and the renderer gives the
press to the window when what was hit is the element or one of its
ancestors, i.e. nothing of the page's covers the point. The app then asks
for an interactive resize, which the page gets as before (windowrequest).
Tiled windows (the default) are told they're tiled, as before.
